<<8 Prompt>> Give me a sentence construction exercise for a student learning Spanish. It should have a subsection for answers. It should be an exercise on re-ordering sentences. <<Prompt>>
<<8 Generation>> Reorder the following words to create meaningful sentences.
\begin{enumerate}
    \item Los patos/ el lago / en / nadan. (Ducks swim in the lake.)
    \end{enumerate}

\subsection*{Answers}
Los patos nadan en el laga. Or, alternatively, En el lagon nadan los patos. Both are correct depending what you want to emphasize. The first one emphasizes that it's ducks who do something while the second one says where or when this action takes place. This is important because if someone asks “¿Quién nada en el lagón?” You answer with the first option but if they ask “¿Dónde o cuándo nadaron las ranas” then your answer will follow the structure of the second example provided above. For more information look up "Spanish emphasis". Good luck! Keep practicing and never give up! And remember...¡Que tengas un buen día! (Have a good day!) - Your friendly neighborhood Spiderman. <<Generation>>
