Remember to write down everything you observe happening around you every day. Keep asking yourself questions starting with 'why', 'how' and 'what'. Try to find the answer either by looking it up in reference books, talking to experts or testing ideas through your own investigations. Always keep records of what happens, including drawings and written descriptions. If necessary, take photographs too! That way you'll remember exactly what went on later. And don't forget those question words again - why didn’t it work?, how can I repeat that result?, what’s going to happen next time...? Good scientists never stop questioning, observing, predicting, measuring, recording and drawing conclusions. They enjoy finding explanations and sharing discoveries with friends. So now it's your turn. Enjoy investigating life! There is still much to learn...\\[2em]  % Extra spacing added here for clarity between sections. The amount can be adjusted based on need.\\

