The total number of non-flat figures is \_\_. Out of these, how many were pyramids? That would be \_\_, right?

And then there's this other type called a 'cube.' There's two kinds of those. How many did we find altogether? We found \_\_ altogether!

How do they differ?
They're all made up differently. One kind has six square faces, twelve straight edges, and eight pointed corners or vertices. What about the second sort? This one also contains six rectangular faces, however its got more edges - twelve that bend and four that don’t plus sixteen pointy spots. Do you think both sorts can roll around your table when pushed gently by your finger? Yes, because each face touches your desk so even pushing one little bit makes it spin around pretty fast sometimes going very speedy while spinning before finally stopping after few seconds later still rolling slightly until completely stationary again soon afterwards too!
