\emph{Presente Indicativo}\\
Indicates actions that occur now or happen regularly. \\
Usage: Talking about habits, daily routines, general truths, facts, etc., as well as future plans when used with "ir" + infinitive verb form.\\
Example:\\
Yo camino por esta calle todos los días. ( I walk down this street every day. ) \\
Ella come plátano todos las mañanas. (She eats banana every morning.)\\
\hlines


\em ph{Pretérito Imperfecto}\\
Describes ongoing or repeated past action without specifying its beginning or end. Usage: Describing conditions of being, states of mind, or descriptions of people/things in the past; also used for incomplete/repeated actions before another specific point in time Example:\\
De pequeño visitaba mi abuelita cada domingo. (As a child, I would visit my grandmother every Sunday). \\
Mis padres viajaban mucho antes de casarse. (My parents traveled a lot before getting married).\\
Mi papá tomaba jugo de naranja todas las mañana ( My dad drank orange juice every morning ). \\
Camila estudió francés durante tres años. Camila studied French during three years.\\



