The total quantity is \_\_. The item with the highest quantity is the \_\_, and the item with lowest quantity is also the \_\. There are as many \_\_ as there are \_\_; however, this amount equals half the sum of all other quantities combined. To find that value simply add them together to get your answer which will be written below.
\begin {equation*} Answer = Total - (\text{Quantity of Crayon} + \text{quantity of Eraser})/2.\end{equation} \\


Answer=\underline{\hspace{5cm}}\\



I have found out how much \_\_\_\_=half of the above answer.

Half Answer=\underline{hspacem{5 cm}}}\\\\

So I can say that Half Answer+Half Answer=Answer.

Therefore:

$\frac{1}{2}$ Answer+$\frac{2}{2}= $answer.

This shows us that $\frac{3}{2 }$ Answer=$\frac{n+ n}{n}$ Answer.

In simple terms we can write it like:
$\frac{(m+n)}{m}= Answer.$

Which leads us to our final discovery:


That’s why when you multiply both sides by m then you end up getting:

$(m+n)=m\times$ answer.



And finally if you subtract $m$ from both sides you will see something magical!


$n=m($answer-1)$. Which means any time you double or triple one side of equation while keeping another intact, you actually multiplied whole expression by two or three accordingly!

Isn’t math beautiful?!!\\
