<<218 Prompt>> Give me a combination of a word problem and an arithmetic exercise for a 4th grade student learning mathematics. It should be an exercise involving calculations. It should have multiple steps. <<Prompt>>
<<218 Generation>> Mira needs to cover a distance of \( 7 \, km\) in one hour.

\begin{enumerate}[label=\alph*.]
\item What is Mira's average speed?
\end{enumerate} 

She has already covered half the journey at this rate when her bus breaks down.
 
\begin {enumerate}[ label= \alph*., continue ]
\item How far does she still need to travel?  
\end {enumerate}

The rest of the way (the remaining distance) takes twice as long because there are road works on that part of the route.

\paragraph {Think With Me}
How can you use what you know about averages to work out how fast she went during those last three kilometers?

\begin[ enumerate ] [ label = \ alph *.,continue ]
   \ item How many minutes did it take her to go these last three kilometres?
    \item At what average speed was she travelling over these last $ 3 \text{km}$?
      \item Over the whole seven kilometre journey,what average speed did she achieve?
       \ end{enumerate }   % END OF ENUMERATE


Now calculate your answers:

\subsection*{Answers}
Average speed calculation:
Speed equals Distance divided by Time; thus Speed equals 7 km / 1 hr which gives us 7 Kilometres per Hour or 7000 meters per Hour since we know that 1000 metres make up a kilometer.


Distance left after covering half:
Since she’s travelled halfway through her 7-kilometers trip before stopping then obviously she must only have 3.5 more Kms to reach where ever she goes.



Time taken for the first four kilometers :
As previously determined she averaged 14 kph so taking our formula from earlier dividing the time by the amount will give us “ t equals d over r” therefore plugging everything into place results with T equals 3500m/14000 m/hr giving us roughly seventeen point fourteen mins traveled in the beginning portion!



Speed throughout final stretch :

We just calculated above that total time taken equaled twenty-six point forty-two min while going only three thousand five hundred meteres meaning if we input them both back into original equation now solving specifically For Rate yields approximately One Hundred thirty-one Point Three Four Meters Per Hour!!


Final Average Speed Calculation : Her overall velocity becomes Seven point Zero Two Five km/h when considering entire distances covered alongside times spent altogether!!!



If anything seems unclear please feel free asking any questions below! Good luck studying math everyone see ya next lesson byebye~!:)! :) <<Generation>>
