What do you notice about subtracting from multiples of ten?

When we take away from a multiple of ten we are left with another multiple of nine minus one less than that amount. So if I had taken away four lots of sixes, say 36 – twenty-four I am left with twelve which is eleven nines plus seven. Likewise when I took thirteen away from forty-three I was left with thirty which is twenty-nine plus one. What’s your answer?
