<<269 Generation>> The ratio of the amount of orange juice to the amount pineapple juice needed to make punch is \(5 : 2\). If \(75 \, \text{ml}\) of orange are used how many millilitres of pineapple juice are required?

\subsection*{Answers}
To find out how much pineapple juice is needed we need to calculate it using the given ratio.

Let's say that x represents the unknown amount of pineapple.
We can write this as:

\[
\frac{\text{orange}}{\text {pineapple}} = \frac{5}{2}.
\]
Substituting in known values (the amount of oranges), gives us:
\[
    \begin{aligned} 
        \frac{(75)} {(x)} &amp;= \frac{{(5)}} {{(2)}} \\
         \Rightarrow   \quad (75)(2)&=(5)x\\  
       \Rightarrow     \qquad      x&amp;=\dfrac{(150)}{5}=30  
   \end{aligned}.    
\]So you would require 30 ml of pineapple. \\  

