<<278 Generation>> John had \( \$40 \) in his wallet. He spent some money at the shop and was left with \( \$24 \). What percentage did he spend?

\subsection*{Answers}
The percentage John spent is \( 40\% \). The amount he spent is calculated as follows:
\[ \text{Percentage Spent} = \left(1 - \frac{\$24}{\$40}\right) \times 100\% = (1-0.6)\times 10\%=40\%. \]
So, John spent \( 60\%\) of his original money, which means that the remaining \( 24\% $  would represent the fraction of his total money not spent.
