What percentage represents the value of item \( B \)?

The ratio between \( A \), \( B\),and their sum can also help determine percentages:
\[  
A :B:A+B=45:55:100 
\]  
Therefore,
Item \( A\) takes up \( \frac{45}{100}=45 \% \),
Item \( B   \)\( 55 \% \).
Both values add up to make \( 100 \% \). The proportion illustrates how each component contributes to the whole. In this context, Item \( B  \) makes up \( 55 % \)of the entire collection. This method applies when comparing parts of a group or set, as seen with ratios like \(1 :2 \)or \(7 :8  \).

