To solve problems in computing we need to break down big issues into smaller pieces – like breaking down large numbers into tens and units. We also need to repeat ourselves sometimes, doing the same thing lots of times until something is complete. Sometimes parts will stay exactly the same throughout our solution. Other parts though must change every single time. Here are some questions to test yourself against all this new information:

When solving a problem in computing, what needs to happen to the bits that stay the same?

What has to happen with the parts that change each and every time? Think about games too!

