<<384 Generation>> Arun sold 16 boxes of flowers on Saturday. He sold twice as many boxes on Sunday.

\begin{enumerate}[label=\alph*.]
\item How many boxes did he sell altogether?
\end{enumerate}

He had 6 more boxes left over than the number he sold on Saturday.

\subsection*{Answers}
He sold \( 16 \times 2 = 32 \) boxes on Saturday, so in total he sold \(16 + 32 = 48\) boxes.
The leftover box amount is \( 6 + 16 = 22 \). Therefore, Arun has 22 boxes left after selling. The final answer to how much was sold altogether remains at 48. No further calculations are required beyond what's provided above. <<Generation>>
