\subsection*{Answers}
The perimeter of an irregular polygon can be calculated by adding up all its sides.
For example:
\( P_{irr\_polygon}= AB + BC+ CD+ DA=10 +7+6+5=28cm\) \\
In case you don’t know how many centimetres are in one meter – here’s your hint: there are \(100cm\) in every single metre!
Therefore,
1 m 92 cm = (1 x 100) cm + 92cm =190 cm.  

To find out what percentage something represents when compared against another value - simply divide that first amount by this second number; multiply result times hundred percent symbol (%) :that's it!!

Here we go :
80 /200 *100% =40%
