If a pizza parlor sells small pies with diameters measuring 14 inches and medium-sized pizzas whose radii equal five inches, determine respective circumferences these round food items.



Pizza circumference calculation:

Small Pizza Circumference: C = π d = 3.14159 × 14 = 43.98 inches

Medium Pizza Circufernce: C=π r=3.1459×(2∗radius)=31.4159 inch

