Write these numbers with words. For example, instead of writing ‘1000', write 'one thousand'. If you live until you're seventy years old, that would mean about another two point four five billion more people sharing our resources! That is roughly three times the current number of Chinese people. The United Nations estimates that it could take between twenty-five and fifty-two years before global populations peak – which might happen sooner if everyone takes family planning advice from David Attenborough:

‘We need to reduce our consumption of everything.' Sir David At- ten borough

However, some scientists suggest we may have already reached Peak Child because most countries' birth rates show falling child numbers. We should note here that predictions can go wrong; we must keep checking against real-life events. One prediction was incorrect: Thomas Malthus forecasted food production wouldn't increase fast enough so he predicted mass starvation across Europe by 1850 ce. He didn't account for farming technology improvements though, such as better seeds. Today half the crops grown worldwide use those improved varieties developed through science since his time. Another improvement has been irrigation systems to distribute water around farms efficiently without wasting precious drops. Other technologies include machinery like tractors, ploughs, balers, combine harvesters plus drones equipped w/cameras monitoring crop health & growth stages via satellite imaging services provided companies including Planet Labs based San Francisco California USA John Deere headquartered Illinois USA Granular farm software tool integrated w/Deere equipment enabling farmers optimize planting fertilizer application decisions using collected information analyzed give insights into best practices yield maximizing potential future generations continue finding ways improve agricultural productivity sustainably meet needs human population expected grow nine billion 2050. The challenge ahead lies balancing increased output while minimizing impact upon environment. This requires adopting methods reducing waste pollution protecting biodiversity maintaining ecosystems supporting local economies ensuring fair labor standards globally among other considerations sustainability long term thinking beyond immediate gains profit maximization short sightedness lead unsustainability eventually collapse entire system unless changed course soon. Remember every small action counts when millions individuals working together create significant positive difference planet deserves thrive not j