<<493 Generation>> Mr. Wu bought 8 kg of fish at \$9 per kilogram. He sold them at \$15 each. How much profit did he make? What was the selling price per kilo? Find his total cost, total revenue, and overall profit.

\begin{enumerate}[label=\alph*.]
\item Calculate Mr. Wu's total cost.
\item Determine Mr. Wus' selling price in terms of kilograms based on the provided information that he sells each unit (kg) at $15.
\end{enumerate} 

Profit = Total Revenue - Total Cost  
Total Profit = \_\_\_ dollars  

Selling Price Per Kilo = \$_{\text{selling}}/\text{kilograms}= \frac{}{}. Selling Price Per Kilos is \$12/kg. The answer to this question should be left blank as it depends on previous calculations not directly addressed here).  



Now you have all your answers fill out the following table below:

| Description | Value |
|-------------|-------|
| Total Cost  |       |
| Selling Price per kilogam |    |
| Overall Profit |        |

Overall profit from buying/selling eight kilograms of fish is $\$48$. This value comes from taking the difference between total revenues ($120) minus total costs ($72), which gives us our final answer above. To find these values we multiplied quantities by their respective prices. Our first calculation gave us the total cost which equaled $72 because $9 times 8 equals seventy-two. Then we found that the selling-price-per-kilo after finding the total-revenue from multiplying fifteen by eight getting one-hundred-twenty-dollars. Finally, subtracting the total-cost from this amount gave us forty-eight-dollas as previously stated. Now with the given information filled into the table below:


