Australia has six states. These states are New South Wales, Victoria, Queensland,
South Australia, Western Australia and Tasmania. It also has two territories – Australian Capital Territory and Northern Territory.

The capital city is Canberra which is located in the Australian Capital territory. The country's population is approximately twenty-two million people. About seventy percent live near the eastern coast where Sydney, Melbourne and Brisbane are situated. Perth, Adelaide and Hobart are other major cities.\\


