Here is a trickier question on fractions: What can you say about the size of the denominator?

Answer: Smaller the better! If it gets bigger then the actual value represented by the whole thing becomes smaller, even if numerator stays constant. So when comparing two equal-sized numerators, we should choose the smallest possible denominator since that gives us biggest overall value out of them all!

