<<592 Prompt>> Give me a grammar exercise for a student learning Spanish. It should be an exercise on completing sentences. It should be a with Answer. <<Prompt>>
<<592 Generation>> Complete these sentences using the verb “Estar.”  
\begin{enumerate}
    \item Ellos \_\_ casados desde hace veinticinco años.
    (They have been married for twenty-five years.)
    \end{enumerate}

\subsection*{Answers}
Ellos están casados. / They are married. / Ils sont mariés. \\

\begin{sidenote} The tense used in this sentence is called "present perfect" and it's formed by combining the verbs estar + main action in its past participle form, which indicates that something started before now but continues up to the present moment. This tense can also be translated as they've been or has/have/it been -ing since... I hope you find useful these clarifications! :) \end{sidenotetext} <<Generation>>
