Remember you must always double or halve one number only! You could do more than one doubling/halving if that helps!

Halves and doubles are easy to work out because they are multiples of ten but some other numbers may need different strategies like near-doubles or near-halves as shown here below. For instance, let's look at how we might calculate $17 \times$.

One way is by calculating half of seventeen first which equals $\frac{17}{2}=8.5$. Then multiplying by four gives us $34$, thus providing our answer.

Another approach involves recognizing that seventeen is close to sixteen, so we start there. We know that $16\times=$. To get from sixteen to seventeen, we simply add one more, giving us an additional. Therefore, when added together, $+$ results in.

