Copy and complete this sentence using two of your new adjectives:
The child was very quiet because he had been naughty at school and his teacher, Mrs Smith, wasn't talking to him any more! He thought it would be best not to speak until she did as she might get crosser if he said something silly or lazy. She was looking quite happy when she came into the room so maybe that would mean they could have story time after all... \\

Mrs Smith told them about a rabbit who liked to jump over really high walls but one day fell down a deep hole in the ground! The little girl who owned the rabbit didn’t know what to do - her dad was busy fixing their car which was broken and mum was out shopping, buying some food for dinner... \\

But then she heard a faint cry coming from the other side of the wall near where the rabbit must still be sitting. So off she went running back inside calling "Dad help!" But unfortunately just as Dad got there having fixed the old motor bike instead, Mum drove up and ran straight o ver the poor thing before anyone even noticed anything let alone being able to prevent such horror happening right under everyone’s noses!! No wonder no-one saw nor heard nothing unusual going on – too much noise from both machines and general commotion outside while moving stuff around everywhere!!! Just like magic though somehow only its wheel got flat… how weird is THAT?!? (Poor tyre by way!)\\


He didn't think that was true,so he looked again at home.The mother took him to the doctor's surgery to see Dr Jones who told them,"It can happen sometimes." They were relieved and decided to go to the park and play ball games. Then they jumped on trampolines until it started raining. After getting wet they went back home. Mum made hot chocolate to keep them warm. His sister added marshmallows floating on top,which made them laugh happily. Soon they played hide-and-seek behind curtains,under beds,in cupboards,and finally found his hidden toy rabbit safe and sound! \\



