In the above grids we show how you could check your answer using another method called 'chunking' or the 'near multiple strategy'. You would do this after doing the bus stop method.
The chunking way is done like this:
To divide 18 by seven, find out what 1 group of ten and eight ones will make when trying to get as close as possible without going over. Then take away that amount from your original total and repeat until there are no groups left over to continue dividing into tens and units separately before finally subtracting them together at once if needed! And don't forget those leftovers because sometimes things just won't add up perfectly but still leave behind important information which might come handy later on during different problems throughout math class workbooks etcetera... Good luck figuring all these tricky parts though I know it sounds confusing right now maybe try writing examples yourself see below:


