Now discuss all these questions with another pupil who carried out the other action (the one not chosen by yourself). Present your joint answers and opinions to the whole class. Are any members of the public helping to keep Bahrain's roadsides free from litter? Look at pictures taken before and after the beginning of anti-litter campaigns held during recent years. Try to find signs or symbols used to show where litter bins are located. Bring examples into school. Work together as a class. Make lists of places which are often littered with rubbish and those areas where there seems little litter lying around. Can you suggest ways to encourage people to use their litter bins properly? Suggest suitable fines and penalties for careless drivers who drop cigarette ends or throw away food packets onto road verges through open car windows. Think of some posters and advertisements designed to persuade people not to leave litter wherever they go. Display them in class. Write reports describing work done by groups involved in anti-latter drives within your community. Prepare displays based upon your written accounts. Show the class what happens when bottles, tins and plastic containers are buried underground over long periods of time. Use items collected from waste material found near your home and school, such as egg cartons and fruit juice packs. Add water containing various colours representing chemicals inside each container to illustrate changes seen when each kind decomposes below ground level. Compare results observed between glass bottle samples left intact versus crushed ones - note differences! Create presentations explaining steps communities may follow towards achieving cleaner environments; include proposed solutions addressing specific issues faced locally regarding pollution caused primarily due human activities like throwing garbage along highways etcetera. Finally share findings amongst peers via classroom display showcasing efforts made toward beautification initiatives across neighborhoods affected negatively because lack proper disposal methods available everywhere today!   Discuss all these problems with another learner who has prepared information on a different environmental problem in Bahrain. Together present your ideas to the class.

